# HirePath

**AI Interview Coach** — an Ionic + Vue cross-platform app for job seekers
in Kenya. Paste a job description, get tailored interview questions with
sample answers, practice, and receive AI coaching feedback on your
submitted answers. Go Pro with a one-tap **M-Pesa** payment.

---

## Highlights

- **AI question generation** — 3–5 role-specific questions + sample
  answers, grounded strictly in the pasted job description
- **AI coaching feedback** — a rating, a critique and a follow-up question
  for every answer you submit (chat-style thread per question)
- **Freemium** — 3 free practice sessions per month; Pro unlocks unlimited
  sessions and feedback
- **M-Pesa payments** — Safaricom STK Push (Daraja API) with instant
  activation via callback, a status-query fallback, monthly renewals and a
  full payment history page
- **PDF report** — one tap exports your payment history to a PDF
- **Live UI** — Supabase Realtime pushes chat, payment and subscription
  changes to the screen instantly
- **Sign-in options** — email/password (with confirmation & recovery) and
  Google (native on Android via Capacitor, OAuth redirect on web)

## Stack

Vue 3 (Composition API) · Ionic 8 · Capacitor 8 · Vite 5 · TypeScript ·
Pinia · TanStack Vue Query · Supabase (Postgres + Auth + Storage +
Realtime + Edge Functions) · OpenRouter/OpenAI · Safaricom Daraja (M-Pesa)

## Quick start

```bash
npm install
cp .env.example .env        # fill in your Supabase project values
npm run dev                 # http://localhost:5173
```

The app talks to a hosted Supabase project
(`vdrdistisykdigqilnpc`). Everything needed to stand up the backend —
schema, Edge Functions, secrets, cron job, storage bucket — is documented
in [`docs/backend-setup.md`](docs/backend-setup.md).

## Scripts

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `npm run dev` | Local dev server |
| `npm run build` | Typecheck (`vue-tsc`) + production build |
| `npm run preview` | Preview the production build |
| `npm run lint` | ESLint |
| `npm run test:unit` | Unit tests (Vitest) |
| `npm run test:e2e` | E2E tests (Cypress, seeds its own QA user) |

> Deploy/push helpers: `scripts/backend-setup.sh` automates the Supabase
> one-time setup (schema, functions, secrets) — see the backend doc.

